WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:04.601
-John, this is heavy,
this is expensive,

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:06.534
but I'm keeping this.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:08.000
-No, I'm a man of my word,
and, technically,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.868
I don't own it, but it's yours.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:14.434
-So will I hear from lawyers?

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:15.601
-If you don't pick up the phone,
you won't.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.033
[ Laughter ]
Right?

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:19.033
-Are you gonna get in trouble
for doing this?

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.434
-Yes. Of course I am.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:22.901
I can't even go anywhere
with the costume.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.567
They have, like, a person --
like, a person who travels

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:27.367
with the costume, and the helmet
comes in its own thing,

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:28.901
and the person
travels with the helmet.

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:30.067
They're like,
"Here's the costume,

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.000
and then here's the helmet.
Take care of it."

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.801
-I was gonna say --
I was gonna say to you --

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.434
I was gonna make fun of you and
go like, "Oh, do you have

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:36.667
a security guard?"
-No. You made fun of me enough.

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.033
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.968
I was gonna say, do you have
a security guard with you?

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.167
You're John Cena.
You are your own security guard.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.367
-No, it's for the helmet.
It's for the helmet.

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.501
-It's for the helmet.
-That is now not mine

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.734
and wasn't mine in the first
place but now, somehow, you own.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:49.801
[ Laughter ]
-I think it's pretty cool.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.834
I might just do it and just
host the show with it on.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.934
-It's actually really cool,
because the audience

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:56.734
gets to see themselves on TV!
-That's right.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:01:00.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.067
I want to --

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.801
-That's not frosted tips,
but it'll do.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.367
-[ Laughs ]
-We're kind of all winners here.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.467
-That's the next bet.
We've never talked --

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.100
You've been on the show,
I want to say,

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.701
it's almost 15 times now.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.434
We've known each other
a long time, yeah.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:13.667
And we've never talked
about this --

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:14.868
-Thank you, guys.
I appreciate that.

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:15.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.701
-No, we add
the applause in later.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.601
We add the applause in later.
-Okay, cool.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.467
-We do that to the monologue,
as well.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:24.000
We've had you --
You've been a guest 15 times.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.834
We've never referenced
the "You can't see me" move.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:29.467
-Yeah!
-Of where -- Like, what --

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.934
Like, what is the back story?
-Okay. So, for those of you

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:34.601
who don't know,
get the damn Internet!

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:37.000
-[ Laughs ] Yeah!
Of course.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.400
-I am -- I became a superhero
long before donning

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.334
the Peacemaker costume.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.868
I developed a special maneuver
in the WWE,

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.567
called the "You can't see me,"
in which I put my hand

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:49.501
in front of my face and say,
"You can't see me."

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.334
And the reason I did this is,
because while we were making

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:55.133
the album
to which my theme music is on,

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:59.467
my younger brother, Sean,
was always our litmus test.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:01.367
He kind of liked the same music,
and he would never go

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:03.067
to the studio with us, so we'd
come home with our tracks,

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.968
and we'd play it for him,
and he was ruthless, man.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:07.868
He would never be satisfied
with any song.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:11.033
And he heard, "The Time is Now"
and just did this dance

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.868
that Tony Yayo did
in of the G-Unit videos.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:16.434
It was like he put his hand
over his head and just kind of,

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:18.067
like, bobbed his head like that.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.634
-Oh, yeah,
I kind of remember that.

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:20.701
-And I was like,
"Man, what are you doing?

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.200
That looked like --
is ridiculous."

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.234
He's like, "No, no, man.
This is some Tony Yayo dancing,

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:25.434
doing his thing."

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.534
And I'm like,
"I'll do it on TV."

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.734
And he's like,
"I dare you to do it on TV."

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:31.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.734
Little did he know,
I'll do this on TV, so...

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:37.067
It was before then.
-Don't dare John Cena.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:42.200
-So, basically -- basically,
on a dare, by absolute chance,

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.601
I went out there, and I figured
this wasn't visible enough,

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:48.334
so I wanted to do this.
And the term "You can't see me"

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.334
is, like, "Well, you're not
even on my level."

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:53.901
And then, like, years later,
it just overcame

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:56.567
the meme culture,
and now literally I'm invisible.

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.701
People are like,
"Why is Jimmy Fallon

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.934
talking to an empty chair?"
Like, so many people

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.567
are gonna say that.
-Yeah, they really are.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.400
-So I'm invisible now.
-You are invisible.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:08.834
-On a dare!
By accident!

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:11.100
-I want to talk about
"Peacemaker."

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.667
Gosh, it's funny.
-Thank you.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.968
-It is --
It's insane, as well.

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:18.400
-Thank you!
-Is it you or is it James Gunn

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.300
or is it a combo platter
of both?

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.234
-It's James Gunn, for sure.
He's such an unbelievably

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:25.968
gifted story teller,
and I think his ability

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:29.667
to just put together
a great squad -- pun intended.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:32.400
But the mind of James Gunn is --
-He wrote all of these?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.901
-All of these, yes.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.400
-When does he have time
to do all this stuff?

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.100
-Well, so when we all
really got locked down,

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.901
if you saw
"The Suicide Squad" --

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:41.067
-Yeah.
-You know, there's a --

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:42.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:46.601
But Peacemaker's future
is very questionable.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.133
And he called me up
in the middle of lockdown.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.634
He's like, "Hey, man, I want to
do a series on Peacemaker."

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.601
I said, "Hey, man,
isn't Peacemaker dead?"

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:54.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.234
And he was like, "No, no,
I got it taken care of."

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:58.801
I said, "Okay. I'm in.
No problem."

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:01.367
And I just let him go to work,
and he wrote eight episodes

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.434
in eight weeks,
and then we filmed

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:04.601
very shortly after that.

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:07.267
-I will just say this.
Here's where you got me.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:10.334
The opening theme song.
-The big dance number.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:13.834
-Dude, he's not kidding.
-Dare you to skip the intro.

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:15.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:17.467
-You did something
that we've been wanting to do

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:20.634
is bring back the TV
kind of theme-song intro.

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.601
And you come out --
-Not quite "Too Many Cooks,"

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:23.767
but, I mean, it's good.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:26.300
-It is like solid gold
is what I would call it.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.934
Like the show, "Solid Gold."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:31.534
It is like you come out,
full on choreographed dancing.

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:33.267
Full on --
Serious face, by the way.

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:36.467
-Yeah. I mean, you'll all
see it, I hope, on HBO Max.

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
You'll all see it?

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.300
-Every cast member --

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.968
Every cast member comes out
and introduces themselves,

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:45.667
and they're all dancing, too,
and doing these --

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:48.133
It's so silly, I go,
"Oh, my gosh.

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.467
He crushed it already."
Before the show even starts.

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:53.400
Everything's funny.
Your sidekick, your pet --

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.200
-The bald eagle -- Eagly.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.400
-His name is Eagly.
-Yeah, it is Eagly.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.434
Yeah, it is Eagly.
My eagle's name is Eagly.

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:04.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:07.968
-Can we even explain what
"Peacemaker" is all about?

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:10.434
-"Peacemaker" is about
wanting to be a superhero.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:14.634
Peacemaker is a guy who wears a
uniform and has a set of skills

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:18.434
and some helmets that can do
some pretty incredible things.

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:22.434
Peacemaker is an anti-hero
because heroic and true acts

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:26.234
of heroism are virtuous, and
Peacemaker is heavily flawed.

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:27.901
He's a human being,
like all of us,

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:30.534
and he wants so badly
to be accepted

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:33.400
as his perception of himself,
which is a superhero.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.868
-Yeah.
-And that's kind of where

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:36.100
the humor of the show comes.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.033
He's, like,
way out of touch with reality.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.067
He's got his kind of
own lens on life

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:41.968
and in doing so,
offends pretty much everybody.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:44.200
-Yeah.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.267
Here is John Cena
in "Peacemaker."

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:48.734
Take a look.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:50.634
-Why are you in your costume?

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.434
-[ Scoffs ]
Costume...

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:53.934
This is a uniform.

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:56.267
And it's brand-new,
so I've got to stretch it out,

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.000
make it more comfortable
before we go on a mission.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.934
-Maybe I'm stupid,
but why would you even

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:01.801
want to wear that on a mission?

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:03.534
A bright red shirt
and white pants

00:06:03.534 --> 00:06:06.400
aren't exactly conducive
to lurking in the shadows.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.734
-People see this uniform,
it strikes fear in their hearts.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.300
-What people?
The other people

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.334
at The Village People tryouts?
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:15.234
-Why is there
a bald eagle in your car?

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:18.000
-That's Eagly.
You guys ordered without me?

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.968
-Eagly is your pet eagle?
-Yeah.

00:06:20.968 --> 00:06:24.133
-Is your dog named Doggie?
-All right.

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:25.567
-Do you have a daughter
named Daughtery?

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:26.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:28.667
-Jealous of a guy's
pet eagle much?

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:31.167
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:34.467
John Cena, everyone!
"Peacemaker" premieres Thursday,

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:36.467
on HBO Max!
-He looks good.

